{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Parses a string with nested parentheses, returning top-level balanced groups.\n    Ignores whitespace and non-parenthesis characters, and preserves order.\n    \"\"\"\n    result: List[str] = []\n    buffer: List[str] = []\n    depth: int = 0\n\n    for ch in paren_string:\n        if ch.isspace():\n            continue\n\n        if ch == '(':\n            if depth == 0:\n                # Start of a new top-level group\n                buffer = []\n            buffer.append('(')\n            depth += 1\n        elif ch == ')':\n            if depth > 0:\n                buffer.append(')')\n                depth -= 1\n                if depth == 0:\n                    # Completed a top-level group\n                    result.append(\"\".join(buffer))\n                    buffer = []  # Reset buffer for the next group\n            # Else: unmatched closing paren, robustly ignore as per spec\n        # Else: ignore non-parenthesis non-whitespace characters\n\n    # After the loop, if depth is not 0, the input was unbalanced.\n    # Per design, incomplete trailing buffers are ignored.\n    return result"}
