{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return True if any three distinct elements in the list sum to zero, else False.\n    Uses sorting and the two-pointer technique for O(n^2) time.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    l.sort()\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # If the current value is greater than 0, no triplet can sum to zero\n        if l[i] > 0:\n            break\n        # Skip duplicate values for i to avoid redundant work\n        if i > 0 and l[i] == l[i - 1]:\n            continue\n\n        left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = l[i] + l[left] + l[right]\n            if current_sum == 0:\n                return True\n            if current_sum < 0:\n                left += 1\n            else:\n                right -= 1\n\n    return False"}
